docs {
  # POST /api/v1/analyze

  **Plan → compute → synthesize** analytical Q&A over the knowledge
  graph (`AnalyticalQueryWorkflow`). An LLM planner picks up to
  `ANALYTICS_MAX_STEPS` primitives from a 42-primitive catalog
  (counts, centrality, communities, dossiers, temporal dynamics,
  graph quality, risk), each primitive runs deterministic Cypher
  against Neo4j, then an LLM synthesizes the answer.

  ## When to use
  Quantitative / structural questions: «сколько», «кто самый
  центральный», «как связаны X и Y», «что изменилось за неделю»,
  «кандидаты на слияние». For «что говорят документы» use
  `/search/*` instead.

  ## Request body
  - **query** *(required)* — the analytical question.
  - **top_n** *(default 20)* — max rows returned by ranking primitives.

  ## Response 200 — `AnalyzeResponse`
  ```json
  {
    "query": "...",
    "answer": "...",
    "provenance": {
      "route": "catalog",
      "plan_reason": "...",
      "steps": [
        {
          "primitive": "distribution_by_type",
          "params": {},
          "cypher": "MATCH ...",
          "rows": [{"type": "Organization", "n": 54}],
          "row_count": 8,
          "source_chunks": [],
          "truncated": false
        }
      ],
      "elapsed_ms": 6669
    },
    "latency_ms": 6669
  }
  ```

  ⚠️ **Numbers live in `provenance.steps[].rows`** (exact Cypher +
  raw rows); `answer` is an LLM gloss and small models can garble
  figures. See `docs/runbook/graph-analytics.md`.

  ## Related
  Centrality / link-prediction / risk primitives read values
  precomputed by `POST /admin/graph/materialize` — run it after each
  bulk ingest (see Admin → Materialize Analytics).

  ## Errors
  - `401` — auth. `500` — workflow raised (body carries the message).
}
